{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Effect of a 12-week supervised exercise programme on HbA1c in adults with type 2 diabetes: a randomised controlled trial",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Title"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "H. Medic, I. Statistician, J. Nurse — on behalf of the MOVE-T2D investigators",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Author"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Background: Structured exercise improves glycaemic control, but effect sizes in routine care are uncertain. Methods: 240 adults with T2D (HbA1c 7.0–10.0 %) were randomised 1:1 to supervised exercise or usual care. The primary outcome was change in HbA1c at 12 weeks. Results: HbA1c fell by 0.62 % with exercise versus 0.11 % with usual care (difference −0.51 %; 95 % CI −0.70 to −0.32; p < 0.001). Conclusions: Supervised exercise produces a clinically meaningful reduction in HbA1c. Trial registration: ISRCTN00000000.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Abstract"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "type 2 diabetes · exercise · RCT · HbA1c",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "Keywords"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Type 2 diabetes affects over 500 million adults worldwide ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "idf2021"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Guidelines recommend 150 minutes of moderate activity per week, but adherence outside trials is poor.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Methods",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Design and participants",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Parallel-group, assessor-blinded RCT at four centres, reported according to CONSORT 2010 ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "consort2010"
          ],
          "style": "cite",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Inclusion: age 40–75 y, T2D ≥ 1 y, HbA1c 7.0–10.0 %, stable medication for 3 months",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Exclusion: insulin therapy, unstable angina, eGFR < 30 mL/min/1.73 m²",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sample size",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "To detect a difference ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\Delta = 0.4\\,\\%",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " with SD ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\sigma = 0.9\\,\\%",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ", two-sided ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\alpha = 0.05",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and power 90 %:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "n = \\frac{2\\,(z_{1-\\alpha/2}+z_{1-\\beta})^2\\,\\sigma^2}{\\Delta^2} = \\frac{2(1.96+1.28)^2(0.9)^2}{0.4^2} \\approx 107",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:n",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "per arm; 120 per arm allows for 10 % attrition.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Statistical analysis",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The primary analysis used ANCOVA on the intention-to-treat population, adjusting for baseline and centre:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "Y_{i,12} = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1\\,\\text{Tx}_i + \\beta_2\\,Y_{i,0} + \\sum_c \\gamma_c\\,\\text{Centre}_{ic} + \\epsilon_i.",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:ancova",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Missing data were handled by multiple imputation (",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "m = 50",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ") under missing-at-random.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
